The framework must allow future lesson creation without rewriting the UI.

A new lesson should be implementable by providing structured content.

For example, adding a new Noun lesson should require:
- Lesson metadata.
- Objectives.
- Explanation sections.
- Grammar rules.
- Examples.
- Vocabulary.
- Exercises.
- Assessment.
- Wrap-up configuration.

The same lesson renderer and exercise engine should display it.

Support:
- Content versioning.
- Draft and published states.
- Localization.
- Reordering sections.
- Updating explanations.
- Adding examples.
- Adding exercises.
- Adding new exercise types.
- Adding audio and images.

If the backend already provides lesson content, integrate with its existing API.

If an admin/content management interface exists, extend it.

Do not hardcode the course content into UI components.

